    "description": "Next to your CLAUDE.md, Claude Code keeps its own notes with auto memory, based on your corrections and preferences. They live in a per-project folder with MEMORY.md as the index; each session loads up to 200 lines of it. /memory lets you see and edit all of it.",
    "companion_text": "Follow Promptwerk for more Claude workflows, step by step. Based on the Memory and Commands pages of the Claude Code docs; the terminal scene is an animated view, not a screen recording. Per the docs: auto memory is on by default in local sessions and stays on your machine, it isn't shared across machines. Claude Code loads the first 200 lines of MEMORY.md or the first 25KB, whichever comes first. Like CLAUDE.md, auto memory is context, not enforced configuration. To turn it off: the toggle in /memory, autoMemoryEnabled: false in a project's settings, or CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1.",
